        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-14T20:34:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct me if I\u0027m wrong, Daisuke, but pd_dfp_dp_get_pin_mode will return a 0 if get_modep() fails.  Following how we populate the \"amodes\" array, it appears we allocate this during the enter mode phase, which should mean we\u0027re in a DP alternate mode state.  However, from a preliminary glance I\u0027m not sure I find where, after entering the state once on a port, we would fail get_modep() in future calls on the port after the dongle is unplugged.\n\nVijay, could the patch\u0027s test description be more specific?  Does this field return something sane for the following scenarios: nothing plugged in, DP dongle plugged in, non-DP partner (ex. charger, USB hub without display)?",
      "parentUuid": "28330ace_f86abc02",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4975,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 4975,
        "endChar": 33
      },
